# ===== Quest Zone — root .gitignore =====
#
# There is no root-level .env today (assets/js/qz-config.js holds the
# PUBLIC Supabase URL + publishable/anon key directly — that's meant to be
# public and safe to ship, see the comment in that file). This file exists
# so that if a real secret-bearing .env is ever created at the project
# root — e.g. for a future build step or Edge Function — it is protected
# from day one instead of needing someone to remember to add it later.
# (supabase/.gitignore already covers supabase/.env*, supabase/.temp, etc.
# for the Supabase CLI's own local files — this covers the rest of the repo.)

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS/editor junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Node, if a build step is ever added here
node_modules/
